version: "2.0"
description: >-
  @a-company/gnomon-darwin-arm64 — the npm platform package carrying the signed,
  notarized, relocatable Gnomon.app for macOS on arm64 (TD-2026-10-21-758; 8.0 M3,
  T-2026-10-21-030). Public; os darwin, cpu arm64; an optional dependency of
  @a-company/gnomon at the exact same version (scripts/sync-gnomon-versions.mjs).
  Outside the root workspaces (os/cpu would fail npm install on the other arch).

components:
  gnomon-darwin-arm64:
    description: >-
      files are ONLY index.js, Gnomon.app.zip and Gnomon.app.zip.sha256. The zip
      is a ditto -c -k --keepParent archive (npm tarballs drop symlinks and
      modes an app bundle needs) that packages/gnomon/scripts/release-darwin.mjs
      copies in (default for a signed, notarized, stapled release; other
      builds only with --package-dir --allow-unsigned-for-tests); both files
      are gitignored. index.js exports platform,
      arch, zipPath, sha256Path and verifyZip(expected), which checks the zip
      against the sha256 compiled into @a-company/gnomon (appZips), never the
      shipped .sha256. No scripts at all (G-SEC-01); publishing goes through scripts/gate-gnomon-publish.mjs. The pack round trip
      (packages/gnomon/scripts/pack-roundtrip.mjs) proves the zip survives
      npm pack with its layout and framework symlinks.
    path: index.js
    type: package
    tags: [gnomon, distribution, release, darwin]
    related: ["#gnomon-npm-packaging", "#release-darwin", "#gnomon-shim"]
    tests:
      - ../gnomon/test/version-lockstep.test.ts
      - ../gnomon/test/pack-roundtrip.test.ts
